## Porcelain
component-porcelain = Porcelain
component-porcelain-made-of-part = fired white clay (kaolin), quartz and feldspar
component-porcelain-description-novice = White fired ceramic. It does not burn or melt in a flame and hardly conducts heat — that is why crucibles are made of it.
component-porcelain-description-school = A porcelain crucible stands heating up to ≈ 1150 °C. Porcelain conducts heat at ≈ 1.5 W/(m·K) — tens of times less than steel.
